# The kernel's additions (roadmap os-server.md P2): pools of 64; 40 spaces more, whose
# copies a revoke deletes, and a 64 KB retype zeroed in pieces: interrupts never off for
# half a tick, since no delete looks through every slot (D9). tests/programs/additions.asm.
program: additions
define: TEST_CAPS
define: TEST_ADD_POOLS
define: TEST_STRETCH
emulators: bochs mame
match: contains
timeout: 120
---
additions: threads made, all 24 (the old pool held 24 in all): 24
additions: the threads revoked (0): 0
additions: spaces made (40): 40
additions: their copies of an endpoint revoked (0): 0
additions: the space that holds them deleted (0): 0
additions: a 64 KB segment retyped (0): 0
additions: zeroed (0): 0
additions: done
rx286: interrupts never off for 10 ms
